   "output": "You are scoring a draft page against its fact sheet. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse; use only the text below.\n\nBrief the writer received: Write the landing page copy for `sackview`, following the tool page section order.\n\nFact sheet (facts tagged [agent-only] are true but belong in a sources note, a link, or a disclosure on a reader page, or should be left out):\nFact sheet:\n\n1. sackview shows what is inside a ZIP archive before you unpack it.\n2. Each entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n3. Install: `pipx install sackview`.\n4. `sackview inspect photos.zip` lists the archive's entries.\n5. `sackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10` shows the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n6. `sackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'` shows only entries whose names match the pattern.\n7. It displays the total unpacked size so you can check available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n8. It never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n9. Inspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service.\n10. It supports ZIP archives only; other archive formats produce an unsupported-format message.\n11. `[agent-only]` Entry metadata is read through the internal ZipDirectoryReader adapter.\n12. `[agent-only]` Size totals use unsigned 64-bit accumulators.\n13. `[agent-only]` Unsupported formats return exit code 24.\n14. `[agent-only]` The package build copies its command schema from packaging/commands.json.\n\nDraft page:\n<<<PAGE\n# sackview: see inside a ZIP before you unpack it\n\nList archive entries and check their sizes before extracting elsewhere.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nZIP archives only \u00b7 Offline inspection\n\n## Archive inspection\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Commands\n\n### Find the largest entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n\n### Filter by name\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\nShow only entries whose names match the pattern.\n\n## Keys\n\nNo key bindings are specified in the supplied reference.\n\n## Check disk space before extracting\n\nsackview displays the total unpacked size. Use it to check available disk space before extracting the archive elsewhere.\n\n## Good to know\n\n**Archive safety**  \nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n**Privacy**  \nNo archive contents are sent to a service.\n\n**Unsupported formats**  \nOther archive formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code 24.\nPAGE>>>\n\nReport, for every fact id 1 to 14:\n- \"present\": true when the page states the fact, in whole or as its reader-observable effect.\n- \"where\": \"explanation\" when it is stated in the main text; \"sources_note\", \"link\", or \"disclosure\" when it appears only there; \"effect_only\" when the page states only what a reader observes (for example \"it never slows your machine\"), not the mechanism; \"absent\" when not present.\n\nAlso report:\n- \"invented_claims\": each claim on the page that the fact sheet does not support, quoted briefly. Rewording, headings, and calls to action are not claims.\n- \"opening\": {\"first_two_sentences\": the first two prose sentences after the title, quoted; \"names_subject_and_job\": true when those two sentences name the subject and say what it does; \"reason_within_first_120_words\": true when a reason a reader would want it appears in the first 120 words}.\n- \"sentences\": the number of prose sentences and prose list items, not counting headings, code, or table cells.\n- \"fragments\": each of those sentences or list items that has no finite verb, quoted.\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"facts\": [{\"id\": \"1\", \"present\": true, \"where\": \"explanation\"}], \"invented_claims\": [], \"opening\": {}, \"sentences\": 0, \"fragments\": []}",
